<<~ ahu #/purpose>>

!! The controller's handoff ~ one seat, passed in the open

A session that holds the CONTROLLER's seat drives the build toward the roadmap's attractor (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-attractor">>): it briefs lanes, routes their handbacks, pushes green heads, keeps canon and the changelog true, and brings the operator only what changes authority, custody at rest or identity bytes. This carrier holds what a session needs to take that seat: the practice, the state, and the way two live sessions pass the seat while both stand.

Read with it, in order: the boot seed (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot">>), the roadmap's cold start (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/cold-start">>), then #/the-lane-law.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-seat>>

!! The seat ~ what the controller does

* ''It briefs lanes.'' One lane per piece of road, each led by one Claude Opus spirit (the Episkopos), its crew standing as `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes` names. A brief stays short and points at the shared law; it names the lane's ground, the ground it leaves alone, its first line of handback, and where it stops.
* ''It routes handbacks.'' A handback answers with one status line and plain notes. A finding on another lane's ground travels to that lane as a message or a patch; a slot that frees gets filled from the roadmap's order without asking.
* ''It pushes green heads, and only those.'' A lane pushes a throwaway `ci/<lane>` branch through `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>` and reports `MERGE-VERIFY`. The controller pushes a shard-green SHA to the feature branch while no run stands in flight, then reads `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --head <sha> --branch <branch>`: three readings, the shards, the full CI workflow, and the container drivers that run on every push (`held-out.yml`). A red reading routes to the lane whose ground it touches.
* ''It keeps the record.'' Changelog bullets for what a person can do, written after reading `git diff HEAD -- CHANGELOG.md` clean (a shared file committed with another hand's lines once claimed work before it landed). Canon true-ups by a read-only collision of the roadmap against the tree, then hand-applied high-confidence lines.
* ''It decides in forge mode.'' A question reaches the operator only where its answer changes who holds authority, custody at rest or identity bytes and no ruling settles it; otherwise the controller takes a house reading, marks it as one, and builds. A parked item stays parked; a turn ends on an act taken.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-practice>>

!! The practice ~ what every lane keeps, each line earned by a real stumble

* ''A refused command stops the lane.'' Never retry it, reshape it, split it, switch tools for it, or hand it to another spirit. The lane reports it; the controller surfaces it to the operator. A sidestep that reaches the same end counts as a retry.
* ''Edits happen in the lane's own worktree.'' The main tree receives a whole, tested patch by one plain `git apply`, then one plain `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`, after `git status --short` and `git diff HEAD -- <path>` show only the lane's lines. One write per command line. No inline script writes into the main tree. A worktree leaves by a plain `git worktree remove`; where that refuses, it stays and the lane says so.
* ''Never `git stash`'' in any form, `git stash list` included; never `--no-verify`; never a foreground `sleep`, alone or chained: a long run goes in the foreground with a long timeout, or in the background with its completion notice.
* ''Red first, with a control''; a race gets pinned by the product's own event, never by a sleep, a retry loop or load. A load probe lives only as an opt-in triage script under `tools/`.
* ''The plugin bundle and genesis move only by the controller's word.'' A lane that changes `packages/lararium-tw5/` source or tiddlers rebuilds the bundle in the same commit and declares the gap in `genesis/unbaked.json`; one labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` folds every declared row.
* ''Scratch roots alone'' for founding, standing or unlocking (`tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs`, then `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs`); never the operator's homes; never a real passphrase, domain or credential.
* ''After a machine restart'' the session scratchpad empties and every worktree under it vanishes. Durable state lives in git and in the session folder; a resumed lane re-reads its resume sheet, provisions a fresh worktree at HEAD, and rebuilds.
* ''O-takiage'' closes every lane and every settle as `mixed-model-swarm#/the-otakiage` names it.
* ''Fetch before you act, and again before you push.'' Another lane can merge into the work branch between two turns; a lane that pushes past it, or reasons from a stale origin, cures the wrong tree.
* ''A local green proves the tree it read.'' A worktree whose `node_modules` link into another checkout tests that checkout's build; every vitest config refuses a stale or foreign `dist` (`tools/vitest-dist-guard.mjs`). Provision lane worktrees with `tools/provision-worktree.mjs <empty-dir>`.
* ''One red in CI masks every package after it.'' `pnpm test` runs the packages in order and stops at the first red, so a cured red can reveal the next. Before pushing a cure, run the packages that come after it, or read the next CI run whole.
* ''Read the containers' own logs before naming a cause.'' A held-out cell uploads each container's log as an artifact (`gh run download <run> -n <cell>`); tallying each container's own lines split the carriage red where the witness's verdict could not. An in-process reproduction holds one Repo, so it cannot show a defect that lives between a CLI process and a running daemon.
* ''Give a sandboxed spirit the logs it cannot fetch.'' A read-only Codex spirit reaches no GitHub API; fetch the failing job logs and hand it the excerpt, or launch it in the networked scout shape `mixed-model-swarm#/the-launch` names.
* ''A review lands nothing until a second face reads it'' (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-lens-law`): a cheap eye's clean read clears nothing, and a tensioned finding gets measured by running it.
* ''Launch background spirits through the harness's background mode'', never a plain `&`: a plain `&` brings no completion notice, and `pgrep -f <pattern>` matches its own shell's command line.
* ''Shell traps in zsh'': `$R:t` reads as a path modifier, so write `${R}:path`; an unquoted variable holding several paths does not split (use `${(f)VAR}`); a `grep` pattern starting with `<<^` treats the caret as an anchor (use `grep -F`); `rm` on a path built from variables trips the safety check, so remove by literal path.
* ''A corrupt object heals by the operator's hand.'' `git fsck --full` names it; rebuild that pack in a scratch repo from an intact working copy and verify it there (run inside the damaged repo, `verify-pack`'s collision check reads the corrupt copy); the swap into `.git/objects` stays the operator's act.
* ''A worktree that initialized submodules'' refuses a plain `git worktree remove`; prove its files landed, then ask the operator for the `--force`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-lane-law>>

!! The lane law ~ what every lead's brief points at, so a session on any machine reads it here

A session reads this carrier and the roadmap alone; no note outside the repository binds a lane. A lead's brief stays short, names its ground, the ground it leaves alone and where it stops, and points here.

!!! The crew
* ''The crew's seats, shapes and launches'' stand at `mixed-model-swarm`: which lineage holds which seat (#/the-seats), the local and cloud crews (#/the-shapes), the lens law, the Copilot seat's read-only role and budget, and the Codex and Copilot launch lines (#/the-launch).
* A lane hands back plainly: one `<<~ status "…">>` line, then what a person can do (each act BUILT, SPECIFIED with its named caller, or OWED), commits, shards, the fresh reader's findings and how each closed, suites, house readings, canon still stale, changelog bullets owed, slips and refusals, and its span's start, end, commits, rows closed and shards for the speed ledger.

!!! Git
* A git command that writes runs alone on its line. Never `git stash` in any form, `git stash list` included (a PreToolUse hook, `tools/stash-guard.mjs`, refuses any Bash call that reaches it, and `.codex/rules/stash.rules` forbids its prefix to Codex); never `--no-verify`; never touch `.git/config`; never push `feature/*` or `main` (the controller pushes); never `git worktree remove --force`.
* A lead works in its own worktree (`node tools/provision-worktree.mjs <empty-dir>` provisions one: inputs copied, every package built and stamped, no link left pointing into the main tree), and checks `git config core.bare` reads `false` before and after.
* A lead lands from the main tree: it rebuilds and re-stamps every package whose source it touched (`node tools/stamp-build.mjs . --pkg <dir>`), confirms the built CLI answers, reads `git status --porcelain -- <paths>` and `git diff -- <paths>` showing only its lines, then commits with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`. It never commits or reverts a line another hand wrote. A subject reads `lar:///ha.ka.ba/<pkg-or-bag>/<area>/<w1.w2.w3> — plain summary`; `-F`, never `-m`.

!!! Refusals and waiting
* A refused or denied command stops that step. Never retry it, reshape it, split it, switch tools for it or hand it to another spirit; save the work as a patch and hand back at once. The controller surfaces it to the operator.
* No foreground `sleep`, alone or chained. A long run goes in the foreground with a long timeout, or in the background with its completion notice.

!!! Bursts, then shards
* A lane lands a burst of commits, each with its package suites, the typecheck witness and the witnesses it could move run locally, then pushes ONE shard lane over the burst's head (`node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>`) and reports its `MERGE-VERIFY` line. A red burst gets bisected (`node tools/burst-bisect.mjs <lane> <good> <bad>`), never guessed. A live commit says so in its message and ends a burst only where later work builds on its bytes. No e2e file runs locally; the controller alone runs the whole witness fleet.
* Suites run from source under a scratch `HOME` and a scratch `LAR_ROOT`, with `LAR_BAGS` unset. Never `pnpm install` in the main tree. Before landing a test file, the charter and gate-dial funnels and the unbuilt-laws witness run.
* No standing test code produces load; a race gets pinned by a handshake between the parties.

!!! Canon and genesis
* Each commit carries its canon lines; law lives in one carrier and the roadmap points at it. Prose keeps L-Prime and stays evergreen. A carrier re-stamps with `lares meme normalize <file>`, one file per call, never piped. Identity keys in a first fence never change. Never edit `bags/elyncia*`, `ftls`, `sdm`, `wtf`, the boot seed, or the submission-guarded carriers.
* A change that moves a plugin bundle rebuilds and commits the bundle and declares the gap in `genesis/unbaked.json`; only a labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` folds it, on the controller's word. A step that would move bytes a genesis artifact carries stops and reports which bytes move.
* Custody, vault and sealed writes count as destroy-class: scratch roots alone, synthetic names and keys only, never the operator's homes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-cloud-lanes>>

!! The cloud lanes ~ the briefs a cloud session takes by name

A cloud session opens on branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`, stands the house from the boot seed, reads the roadmap's #/the-attractor, #/cold-start and #/rulings, this carrier whole (#/the-lane-law binds it), `working-procedures`, and its lane's kit, then walks its lane below. It leads as the Episkopos over the cloud crew `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes` names.

A cloud lane commits on its OWN branch, `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--<lane>`, cut from `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`, and pushes that branch alone; CI and held-out fire on it. It shards each burst with `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>-<n>` and reads `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --head <sha> --branch <branch>`. Where the container's `gh` holds no login, each burst pushes the lane branch instead: CI's own E2E job runs the same five shards behind its merge gate, and the lane reads CI and held-out through the GitHub connector. The committed `.claude/settings.json` runs `tools/stash-guard.mjs` before every Bash call; a refusal from it stops that step. It never pushes `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` or `main`: the controller merges each lane branch after reading its three readings. Before its final push it merges `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` into its lane branch. It lists canon and changelog lines for the roadmap and `CHANGELOG.md` in its handback, and edits neither. It stops at a clean boundary when context runs short and hands back in the lane law's shape, with its lane branch and head.

!!! Lane `wire-socket` ~ past lane
Train W's assembled cutover landed as PR #44: every vessel socket opens through the sealed face gate on one handshake, fleet join serves every face, a fresh browser device stands at the floor, and a herm answers the knock where a Nexus carries it. The roadmap's `W` rows name what stays owed.

!!! Lane `carriage-fold` ~ a local session's lane
Kit: <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/carriage-fold-lane">>. Roadmap row `W18`: the carrier folds walk the roll anchors (PR #50, merged 2026-10-19), and `P20`'s gate half reads a place contract across a roll (PR #54), so held-out reads green on every driver; DreamDom-Wright builds `F6` on lane `holder-owner`, owing the deliberate cross-epoch held-out cell beside it. A lane under `mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`: its own sub-branch, the work swarm's build pair in one worktree, the other lineage's read, the overwatch, a pull request.

!!! Lane `browser-custody` ~ past lane
Its custody API landed (the roadmap's `B1` row names what it built and what stays owed). Its boot caller rides with whichever lane next holds `open-browser-vessel.ts` and the web boot. The persona roots' seal waits built and red-first on `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--persona-root-seal`: the root mint refuses `no-custody-slot`, so it merges only after that boot binds a slot and unlocks before `openBrowserVessel`.

!!! Lane `kahu-plane` ~ past lane
Train P after N landed: the chartered classes, exact-bytes promotion, Kahu-cabal admission, the co-signed steward map, the re-anchoring fence and the anchored ancestry count, with R-KAHU witnessed across two vessels. The crossroads crossing asks the seats (`P21` built). The roadmap's `P18` to `P20` name what stays owed. `P18` rides with whichever lane holds both vessel composers. `P19` and `P20` wait half-built on `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--gate-ancestry`, its commit message naming the writer and verifier cure that lands them.

!!! Lane `scout` ~ past report
The dated `next-path-scout.md` report records the earlier tree; its top line names the commits that supersede its stale observations.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/state>>

!! State ~ the controller trues this section at every handoff

The merged road carries the fleet-join door on every face, the sealed face gate on every socket, the recovery doors, N's anchor guards and witness, and H's pure delegation and grant; browser custody's API and the Kahu plane after N stand. No cloud lane runs; the controller's local crews take the road, and each new lane opens its own sub-branch and pull request (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`). The `carriage-fold` lane opens next, in its own session.

* ''Closed'': the custody seal train; the disk shore; truthful receipts; container drivers on every push; the seat train (K); side lane S8; fleet join; restore after guardian enrolment; root cards; restore as persona zero.
* ''Train N'': two-vault kapae and roll-anchor doors stand. N2's per-realm edge anchor, N4's prior-roll refusal and N5's two-root charter re-import witness stand. A newcomer's board catch-up of unseen acts stays outside N5.
* ''Train W'': the full route pin, the sealed application frame, `GateSessionChannel` after the verdict, face-scoped sharing, the fleet-shadow consult and the assembled socket cutover stand. Owed: a signed floor card, the floor pin's causal position, two-vault carry, face switching on one device, a fleet-join carry walk in the browser weld, and the founder's own carriage fold, which reads its herms' floor pins as uncarried (held-out herm-mesh and the nexus cell).
* ''Train P'': the chartered classes, exact-bytes promotion Kahu-cabal admission and the crossroads crossing's approval stand built and R-KAHU witnessed; the shared-canon read, cabal acts across a roll and the gates' ancestry stay owed.
* ''Train H'': H2's delegation and three dials and H8's signed grant and public-half verifier stand specified. The live issuer, reader, store, sorter and serving rows remain owed.
* ''Recovery'': guardian sets ride bundles; provisional standing and its view verbs, sealed outbox, root-card restore and restore founding stand. Parcel ship and delete, remaining provisional guards and sibling proof stay owed.
* ''Browser custody'': the slot tree seals the device seed and the Archives, refusal and reopen witnessed; the boot unlock and the passkey slot stay owed, and the persona roots' seal waits on the boot unlock (`B1`).
* ''Instruments'': every vitest config refuses a stale or foreign `dist` before its suites run (`tools/vitest-dist-guard.mjs`). A green shard run reads the e2e sets alone; a lane runs each touched package's whole suite and `tools/witness-all.sh` before it lands, and a new CLI command owes its accepts-table row and the regenerated verbs fixture. Owed: the per-package digest hashes test files too, so a dependency's test edit makes its dependents refuse at the desk until a rebuild; narrowing it to built inputs moves `stamp-build.mjs` and `build-freshness.ts` together. The source-pointer witness refuses an empty census. Two branches wait. `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--instruments` holds four gates that stop passing on prose. Its rite-commands cure reads red on `sensorium-runbook.mem`'s `EmbedderIdentityUnknownWarning`, a name the repo's mempalace copy imports in tests and defines nowhere, so it lands after the sensorium hand re-aims that line. Its mesh-coverage, typecheck and shared code scan owe four cures first: single-quoted union values, a nested template that injects a fake union, a regex literal that masks a real file, and a multi-line TS6059 that reads as a crash. A scanner built on the TypeScript compiler closes the last three as one class. `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--symbol-anchor-truth` counts a name as defined only by a declaration in code, reading the shared code scan, so it rides on `--instruments` and lands with it; its stricter count reads 34 on the span, and it sets its own ceiling when it lands.
* ''DreamDOM (train D)'': the model stands in `docs/pono/dreamdom` and its phases in `docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap`. D0 (the harness, the engine mends, the worker-side and stock-tab baselines) and D1 (the camera contract: `lar:` kinds on the island wire, keyed frames under a mount epoch, answered acts, declared cancellation, the toggle family, root services, the three page controls with the IME rules, files, drops, order, keys and routes) stand, with the thirteen interaction goldens green on the engine and page harnesses and the daemon surface's talk-story in `docs/pono/daemon-surface`; each phase's row names what stays owed. Genesis carries the house plugin whole. D2 (the record port) comes next; `dreamdom-seed#/head` names where the train stands for the session that takes it.
* ''The road ahead'' (each row in the roadmaps names its owner; one lane per row, opened under `mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`):
** Wave one, on disjoint ground: `mesh-goldens` (`docs/pono/mesh-goldens`, the e2e suite rewritten as scripts of acts and journal events; the journal, `lares events` and `W24`'s script stand, and the next slice lays readiness entries and moves the next family of scripts onto the journal); `carriage-fold` (`W18`, kit `docs/pono/carriage-fold-lane`), whose red test also cures the held-out herm-mesh and nexus cells; D2's pure slices (the recording document with its serialisers, the width and local-filter core), each red test drawn from the field's five contract questions; `instruments`, a scanner built on the TypeScript compiler that lands `--instruments` and `--symbol-anchor-truth` together.
** Wave two: the rest of D2 on the island protocol (the port kinds, the invoke gate, presence); `B1`'s boot unlock and passkey, which unparks `--persona-root-seal`; the wire's owed rows `W14`, `W15`, `W16`, `W21` and `W22`; `W26` (the system wikis release on the crossroads and every other wiki reads the floor through `@oracle`), with `W21` riding it; `W25` (the carried bag event's creator in the clear) lands before wave three.
** Wave three: `P18` to `P20` on `--gate-ancestry`; D3's glass engine and three-boot spike; E, H and the sealed store's later steps.
** Then the operator founds the persistent node vessel by hand.
* ''Rulings the crew still needs from the operator'': D3's default width, after the three-boot spike; DreamDOM's key grain, its interaction goldens family and its `core` charter (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`); the moʻolelo's blessing. The rulings of 2026-10-16 stand in `stable-founding-road#/rulings` and `dreamdom#/open-rulings`.
* ''Shared ground'': lanes meet on the two vessel composers; one lane at a time holds a composer hunk, and the others hand theirs to the controller as a patch.
* ''The crew'': each lane runs the work swarm, a Sonnet Episkopos, one Sol and one Copilot `gpt-5.3-codex` seat at medium effort, each seat building or reading as the work pulls, and the Opus controller reads every chunk's diff before it merges; a Copilot PR review runs only when the operator asks for one (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes`).
* ''The Copilot allowance'': 300 premium requests a month on a legacy annual plan, resetting on the first; the Chao pair costs about one request per burst, and a PR review, about 13, runs only on the operator's ask.
* ''The operator's focus'' (2026-10-18): the DreamNet and the browser's capabilities. The art-sigil carriers (`docs/art-sigils/`, PR #47) stand set aside, off this road.
* ''The span head'' (2026-10-19): CI reads green at `fc1e442f7`, #49's merge, shard 2's ③ gone with the shared pointer. Held-out reads red on herm-mesh and the nexus cell alone, waiting on `P20`'s gate half. Merge order in flight: #50 (merged), #52 (`W26` slice 2), #51 (G37's lifts), then #53 (the evergreen witness) last, so its ceilings count what the span holds. The restore file of the branch sweep burns on or before 2026-10-31.
* ''The sensorium rests'' (operator, 2026-10-19: //"Pause sensorium work, unhook their tests for now. Focus on the DreamNet & DreamDom work"//). The mempalace-integration crew stands paused, and CI runs no sensorium Python suite until that lane resumes and re-hooks it (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`). The suite's last CI reading: one red, `test_guest_ward.py`, which names `trial_serving.py` for naming the guest install without calling `refuse_guest`; the cure is that call, left for the lane. A local run reads 21 reds this machine's live palace may account for, still unsorted.
* ''The controller's crucible names what it leaves out'' (2026-10-19). It runs `tools/witness-all.sh` over a scratch merge and reads each lane's shard verdict; it runs no CI-only suite (the sensorium's Python suite, the held-out cells), so it reads `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs` on the span head before each push, never after, and reads the lane's own verdict (`--branch <lane> --head <sha>`, CI and held-out both) before it merges: held-out runs on a pushed lane branch alone, and PR #55 merged over a held-out red its lane head already carried (`mesh-scenarios-meme`, a `LOAD` into system canon that `W27` refuses). A shard runs no witness, so a lane runs `witness-all` itself before it hands back: a rename the roster witnesses track reads red there first.
* ''Merge trains'' (operator, 2026-10-19: //"run the merge trains"//). A lane stays as strict as before: red-first per commit, its own suites, its own `witness-all`, shards, and its own CI and held-out read green. The controller then merges ready lanes in TRAINS: when two or more read ready, or every few hours, it merges them onto one scratch integration head, runs one crucible (`witness-all`) over the combined tree, places canon once, and pushes the span once. A red train bisects by re-running only the failing witness over each lane's merge in turn. Before merging, a train lists each pair of lanes that share a file, since held-out on the span reads only after the push, and it runs the whole suite of every package two of its lanes both touch over the combined tree: train two's crucible ran witnesses alone, and `bag-doc-holds-across-boots` (#68) read red on the span once #67, renaming the cap-event rows that test counted, merged beside it. A train reads the SPAN's own head first, CI and held-out both, and never merges onto a red span: three span runs read red under two trains while each train read only its lanes (#69's cure, then a racing test control that #77 seeded). A lane built jointly runs the crucible before any Wright builds on it: the atom cut's floor boot read red only once its browser half joined. A held-out cell reruns only with its whole run, since a lone cell's rerun seeks an image its attempt never built. The Wrights take range mandates (a row's several slices, one PR per coherent slice, handed back once) and stop for a design fork, never for a merge.
* ''A reused image measures the day it was built'' (2026-10-19). `household-https-witness` builds `lares-surface:local` only when the tag stands absent, so an image from 2026-10-14 read red against a CLI that has since gained `vessel found --hearth --name`, and the red read as environmental for days. Rebuilt from the span (`docker build -f Dockerfile --target serve -t lares-surface:local .`), the witness reads every assertion held. Lead: the witness refuses an image older than the source it would serve, rather than reusing it.
* ''Leads from the controller's reads'' (2026-10-19): an engine that leaves and returns re-alerts under the same request id, which matters only where a request id dedupes (`engine-watch.ts`); a realm grant's cap proof is a bare `ok`, so a receipt names no authority (`meme-verbs.ts`).
* ''A flake stands named'' (2026-10-19). `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/herm-carriage-gate-native.test.ts`, its CONTROL "a place the Nexus carries presents its counted contract and reads the map, verified", read "dial failed: the gate said nothing" once at `365148e5a`, a merge that touched no package code, and read green on the re-run of the same head. Measured and cured (PR #59): the test's pull helper raced an honest pull against 400 event-loop turns, so a loaded runner cut it short; it now waits on the gate's own outcome.
* ''The branch sweep'' (operator-run, 2026-10-18): every fully merged, patch-equivalent, squash-merged and harvested branch left, local and origin. Standing beside `main` and the span: the lane branches, the parked lanes (`--gate-ancestry`, `--instruments`, `--persona-root-seal`, `--symbol-anchor-truth`), `fold-prep-local`, `backup/remove-sqlite-before-rewrite`, `github-pages` (the operator's own, off the controller's list); `worktree-agent-a522be6155f677695` left on 2026-10-18 once its commit read replayed on the span (`ea5027586`); `ci/ctl-gjd-5` left once its five patches read carried on the span. The restore lines rest in the session folder's `lane-artifacts/`, to burn before any `git gc` could prune their objects.
* ''Lane W26'' (kit `docs/pono/w26-floor-lane`): the operator ruled the architecture and its leans on 2026-10-18 (one owner per registry; the floor reads by CID), and the kit names six slices. Branch `--w26-own-canon` holds the measurements that drew it (the shared-oracle probe, the `W25` creator probe) beside a recipe-watch hold that lands nowhere, since slice 2 removes what it holds against. The release signs under its own domain, `floor-release` (operator-approved). DreamNet-Wright builds slice 1 on `--w26-floor-1`, the genesis bake on the controller's word.
* ''Lane `browser-secrets`'' (`B1`, PR #48): persona roots and every face secret rest sealed under the slot tree, and `standBrowserCustody` asks per tab. Its composer patch (web boot, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `custody-clear`) waits for the controller once the PR's CI reads, then a two-tab check by the operator.
* ''Ground'': each remaining loop names its owner in the roadmap.
* ''The operator's own founding'': the persistent node vessel founds after the roadmap's work and its aftermath land, by hand, on a TTY; no spirit founds it. The two-hearth ceremony, HARBOR's live steps and the hardware choice for unattended ember raises stay the operator's hands.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-live-handoff>>

!! The live handoff ~ two sessions, one seat, passed by word

A session can close and a fresh one boot from carriers; a ''live'' handoff lets both stand for a while, so the new seat can ask the old one what no carrier caught. The seat passes by explicit word, never by drift.

# ''One controller at a time.'' Only the seat-holder pushes the feature branch, fills lane slots and commits to `CHANGELOG.md` or the roadmap. The other session reads, asks, and works only lanes the seat-holder hands it by name.
# ''The outgoing seat trues #/state'' in this carrier, commits it, and names its lanes in flight: which will finish under it, and which pass to the incoming seat with their resume sheets.
# ''The incoming seat reads first'': the boot seed, the roadmap's cold start, and this carrier whole, #/the-lane-law included. Then it asks the outgoing seat, by session name over the message channel, whatever stays unclear: a lane's intent, a house reading's reason, a red that looked like a flake.
# ''The seat passes by message.'' The outgoing seat sends "the seat passes to <session>" once no push stands in flight and every lane it keeps has a named owner; the incoming seat answers "the seat holds". Until that answer, the outgoing seat still holds it.
# ''Lanes keep their spirit.'' A running lane answers the session that launched it. A lane that passes gets a new lead launched by the incoming seat from its resume sheet, never a message to a subagent of another session.
# ''Questions flow both ways after the pass''; the outgoing session may keep a lane to finish, and reports its handback to the new seat-holder as a lane would.

<<~/ahu>>

